---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Website Use & Privacy | Donovan Family Dentistry"
  description="Website-use, privacy, administrative-inquiry, emergency, insurance, and document guidance for Donovan Family Dentistry."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Website use & privacy</p>
      <h1>Use the website for general information—not private clinical communication.</h1>
      <p class="lead">This page explains the safety boundaries built into the production-candidate website.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h2>General information only</h2>
          <p>Website content is educational and administrative. It does not establish a dentist-patient relationship, replace an examination, provide a diagnosis, or create an individualized treatment plan.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h2>Urgent concerns</h2>
          <p>Do not rely on a website message for urgent dental or medical concerns. Call the office at <a href={`tel:${site.phoneHref}`}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a>. Call 911 or seek emergency care for difficulty breathing or swallowing, severe uncontrolled bleeding, or a serious face or head injury.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h2>Administrative inquiries</h2>
          <p>The website request form is limited to name, contact details, reply preference, a general topic, and a short administrative message. Do not enter symptoms, diagnoses, medications, insurance identifiers, Social Security numbers, treatment details, photographs, files, or medical history.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h2>Preview and delivery</h2>
          <p>In the private production-candidate build, the form previews the message locally and sends nothing unless an administrator separately enables and configures the protected delivery service. Live delivery remains a launch blocker until office-owned accounts, recipients, retention, response ownership, anti-spam controls, and a real delivery test are approved.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h2>Insurance and payment</h2>
          <p>Benefit information and estimates are not guarantees of payment. Coverage, financial responsibility, payment options, and office policies must be confirmed directly with the practice and the patient's plan before treatment.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h2>Patient forms and local files</h2>
          <p>Fillable PDFs are completed on the visitor's device. The website does not upload a completed medical-history form. Save and print forms only on a trusted device, and bring them to the office unless the practice provides an approved secure delivery method.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h2>Analytics and technical logs</h2>
          <p>Optional privacy-preserving site analytics are disabled unless the website administrator configures them. Hosting and security providers may maintain ordinary technical logs needed to deliver and protect the site; website code is designed not to place administrative-message contents into analytics or GitHub.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h2>Privacy practices</h2>
          <p>The practice's Notice of Privacy Practices is available as a separate patient document. <a href="/forms/privacy-practices.pdf">Open the Notice of Privacy Practices</a>.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h2>External services</h2>
          <p>Directions and other external destinations are governed by their own terms and privacy practices. Confirm addresses, availability, and policies directly before relying on third-party information.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 2rem"><strong>Last reviewed:</strong> August 1, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
